# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own value to enable the
# "Continue with Google" button on the landing page. Without it, the landing
# page still works fully — that button just renders disabled with an
# explanatory tooltip, and "Try Solace free" always works with no setup.
#
# How to get a client ID:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   2. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "Web application"
#   3. Add your site's URL (e.g. https://solace-ebon.vercel.app) under
#      "Authorized JavaScript origins" — no redirect URI is needed, this
#      uses Google Identity Services' token flow, not a redirect.
#   4. Paste the generated client ID below.
#
# If deploying on Vercel, set this as an Environment Variable in the project
# settings instead of committing a real value here.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Server-side only, used by api/cloud-chat.ts to call an OpenAI-SDK-compatible
# cloud AI provider for the optional cloud model. Deliberately NOT prefixed
# with VITE_ — that would bundle it into the public client JS and expose it
# to anyone who opens the browser's Network tab. Without these set, the
# cloud model option simply stays unavailable; everything else still works.
#
# If deploying on Vercel, set these as Environment Variables in the project
# settings instead of committing real values here.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=
